# Single source of truth for the SPARQL Anything build used by the pipeline.
# Sourced by map.sh (host + container runtime) and by the Dockerfile (build-time download).
#
# Pinned to the stable v1.2.0, which carries the fx:slice.size and fx:csv.quote-char fixes that
# config/places.rq relies on (SPARQL-Anything/sparql.anything#624 and #625). It requires Java 21.
# We previously pinned a nightly (snapshot-<date>-<time>) because it was the first build carrying
# those fixes, but nightly releases are pruned upstream after a few days: the tag disappeared and
# the pipeline downloaded a 404 page as bin/*.jar (“Invalid or corrupt jarfile”). RC and stable
# tags are permanent, so never pin a nightly here. The only commits between v1.2.0-RC1 and v1.2.0
# are documentation and the Java 21 bump, and the two builds behave identically on missing and
# unparseable inputs.
#
# The version tag and the jar filename differ (the stable jar keeps the ‘v’, the RC did not), so
# both are set explicitly.
#
# The := defaults let an external environment variable override the pin (e.g. to test
# another build) without editing this file.
: "${SPARQL_ANYTHING_VERSION:=v1.2.0}"
: "${SPARQL_ANYTHING_JAR:=sparql-anything-v1.2.0.jar}"
